<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · site</p><h1 class="enc-title">Madriu-Perafita-Claror Valley</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Madriu-Perafita-Claror Valley is a glacial valley in south-eastern Andorra, covering almost a tenth of the country's territory. Inscribed in 2004 as Andorra's only <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/unesco-world-heritage-site">UNESCO World Heritage Site</a>, it preserves a cultural landscape of summer pastures, stone shepherds' huts, terraced fields, tracks and traces of iron smelting that shows how people used high-mountain resources over a thousand years. No road runs through it.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/madriu-perafita-claror-valley.jpg" alt="Madriu-Perafita-Claror Valley" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Aliento Más Allá · CC BY 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Refuge_perafita_andorra.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
